# L §4.2: "A day in added may be a hole or a window ... every day known but one"; L §8.1 HOLE-CALENDAR: "an added
# day that is a hole or a window decides the result", its question "the added day's question".  A Monday that is
# otherwise a business day may be the added day: a hole; a Saturday is no business day whatever the added day is.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input len: calendar

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2025-12-01
  len = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [?"which day is the bridge day?"])

ask q1: is_business(2026-03-02, len), is_business(2026-03-07, len)
=== expect
q1: (?"which day is the bridge day?" (len), false)
  cut 2026-12-31
